'''''Solanum emulans''''', commonly known as '''eastern black nightshade''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Solanaceae]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Solanum emulans Raf. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:819111-1 |access-date=2025-03-25 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref> It is native to all Canadian provinces (except British Columbia) and nearly all of the United States (except the Pacific coast states and Nevada), and it has been introduced to scattered locales in Europe.<ref name=":0" /> There have been considerable taxonomic difficulties associated with this widespread taxon and its relatives ''[[Solanum americanum]]'', ''[[Solanum nigrum|S. nigrum]]'', and ''[[Solanum villosum|S. villosum]],'' all of which are in the subsection ''Solanum'' of the genus ''[[Solanum]]''.<ref name="Tiina_Särkinen">{{cite journal |last1=Särkinen |first1=Tiina |last2=Poczai |first2=Peter |last3=Barboza |first3=Gloria E. |last4=Van Der Weerden |first4=Gerard M. |last5=Baden |first5=Maria |last6=Knapp |first6=Sandra |date=2018 |title=A revision of the Old World Black Nightshades (Morelloid clade of ''Solanum'' L., Solanaceae) |journal=PhytoKeys |issue=106 |pages=1–223 |doi=10.3897/phytokeys.106.21991 |pmc=6070582 |pmid=30072843 |doi-access=free}}</ref><ref name="Sandra_Knapp">{{cite journal |last1=Knapp |first1=Sandra |last2=Barboza |first2=Gloria E. |last3=Sarkinen |first3=Tiina |date=2017 |title=(2546-2547) Proposals to reject the name ''Solanum rubrum'' and to conserve the name ''S. alatum'' with a conserved type (Solanaceae) |journal=Taxon |volume=66 |issue=4 |pages=988–989 |doi=10.12705/664.21 |doi-access=free}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |title=Report of the Nomenclature Committee for Vascular Plants: 71 |date=2020 |last1=Applequist |first1=Wendy L. |journal=Taxon |volume=69 |issue=2 |pages=391–397 |doi=10.1002/tax.12217 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

